Z||000000||MD_Fiero||08-27-2001||03:50 PM||||take oout the locking mechanism out of the black piece of the door with the door opener on it?...also..how do i get the manuall window roller thingy off?..thanx||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-27-2001||05:01 PM||||The black lock knob I believe has to be pryed out with a screw driver as it sits on a rod that has a 90% bend on it that goes in a hole that is in back of the black plastic knob. the window handle you need a tool from auto zone sells that you use to push out a retainig clip that holds the handle on to the shaft shoud be diagram on the back of package this tool will cost 4 maybe 5 dollors.hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||MD_Fiero||08-27-2001||10:44 PM||||yes...helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Thanks alot!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||08-27-2001||11:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B>The black lock knob I believe has to be pryed out with a screw driver as it sits on a rod that has a 90% bend on it that goes in a hole that is in back of the black plastic knob. the window handle you need a tool from auto zone sells that you use to push out a retainig clip that holds the handle on to the shaft shoud be diagram on the back of package this tool will cost 4 maybe 5 dollors.hope this helps</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Or do it the easy way, run a shop rag between the knob and door panel, it should snag the clip and pull it out...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jaxx||08-29-2001||12:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierowrecker:<BR><B> Or do it the easy way, run a shop rag between the knob and door panel, it should snag the clip and pull it out...<BR>crash...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damn... where were you with this advice when I needed it a month or so back?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Getting mine off was such a pain in the a$$ since I had no clearance for a screwdriver. I should have bought the tool, had I thought about it.<P>Jaxx<BR>'86 GT work in progress<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jaxx||08-29-2001||12:58 AM||||Actually, once you've unscrewed the black door plate, the locking rod detaches pretty easily from the locking knob. In my experience, getting the rod and knob to stay aligned during reinstallation is trickier, but still not difficult.<P>Jaxx<BR>'86 GT work in progress||||reg||1
